    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 8
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cluster: severe unilateral periorbital pain (15 min–3 hr), with ipsilateral autonomic features (tearing, rhinorrhea, ptosis, miosis, conjunctival injection). Occurs in clusters; predominantly males. Mechanism: hypothalamic activation + trigeminal"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "-",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 8
        }
       }
      ],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 8
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Secondary HA: arise from underlying cause (bleed, tumor, infection, raised ICP) — carry red flags (worst HA ever, positional, wakes from sleep, fever/meningismus, focal deficits, papilledema). Normal neuro exam = primary; abnormal = secondary → imaging"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
