    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 8
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Peripheral (inner ear / CN VIII): episodic, positional (BPPV, vestibular neuritis, Ménière’s); fatigable unidirectional nystagmus; +Dix-Hallpike; no focal neuro deficits; benign"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "-",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 8
        }
       }
      ],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 8
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Central (brainstem / cerebellum): non-fatigable, direction-changing or vertical nystagmus; accompanied by focal neuro deficits; causes = stroke, MS, tumor → DANGEROUS, requires emergent workup. HINTS exam: Head Impulse (normal in central) + Nystagmus direction + Test of Skew"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "-",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 8
        }
       }
      ],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 8
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Clarify “Dizziness”: vertigo (spinning) vs presyncope (lightheaded/woozy/about to faint) vs disequilibrium (off-balance). Positional changes → BPPV/vertigo or orthostatic syncope"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
