    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 8
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Brain regions: Cerebrum (2 hemispheres; frontal, temporal, parietal, occipital lobes) — higher functions. Cerebellum — coordination, balance, fine motor. Brainstem (midbrain, pons, medulla) — relays signals, CN nuclei, involuntary functions. Diencephalon = thalamus, hypothalamus, epithalamus. Meninges = dura, arachnoid, pia (blood collects in epidural, subdural, or subarachnoid spaces)"
     }
    ]
   },
